WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.970
After 20 years, I've learned the hard way

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.860
that there was never a good
time to withdraw US Forces.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.250
How many more generations of
America's daughters and sons

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.780
would you have me send to
fight Afghanistan's civil war

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.420
when Afghan troops will not?

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.030
President Joe Biden's decision

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.120
to pull the United States
military out of Afghanistan

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.670
after two decades

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.410
has been roundly condemned
by interventionists

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.560
who say that the retreat was humiliating

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.350
and disastrously planned

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.170
leaving thousands of Afghans
prey to vengeance and violence

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.070
at the hands of the Taliban.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.430
For Scott Horton and other
critics of US foreign policy,

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.520
the biggest question about the withdrawal

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.160
is what took so long?

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.500
Horton heads up the Libertarian Institute,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.600
is editorial director at antiwar.com

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.980
and host the Scott Horton show podcast.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.520
He's also the author of Enough Already

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.530
Time to End the War on Terror.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.010
Recent talk with Horton about
why American intervention

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.940
in Afghanistan was doomed from the start

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.680
and how a libertarian
approach to both domestic

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.770
and foreign affairs would
make people better off

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.133
all over the globe.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.490
Scott Horton, thanks
for talking to Reason.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.810
Happy to be here.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.130
Just before we started talking Joe Biden,

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.770
President Joe Biden
explained his rationale

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:23.500
for withdrawing from Afghanistan right now

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.440
and in the manner that he did.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.450
What did you think of Biden's
defense of his policy?

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.420
I think it was perfectly reasonable.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.110
I mean, I don't know what
else he was supposed to say

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.490
in the circumstances.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.170
It's far too late to start
the war all over again

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.270
or anything like that.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.250
If anything, you know, really,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.120
the biggest weakness of his policy

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.080
has been that he broke
the deal essentially.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.120
The deal that Donald Trump had signed

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.500
said, we will be out by May 1st.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.810
And I think just for political reasons,

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.820
he didn't want it to
be Trump's withdrawal.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.600
He wanted it to be his own thing.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.010
And so he delayed that.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.710
But that just gave the
Taliban this much more time

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.570
to take over the entire country

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.630
as America's on their way out the door.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.660
So that's the reason
for the big scandal now

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.980
is we didn't get our decent interval.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.680
We're supposed to be able to leave

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.470
and then they are supposed
to give us a few weeks

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.210
before embarrassing us this badly

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.150
by taking over the
whole country like this.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.070
You know, let's get to
Biden in a second too.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.570
You know, everybody in the
news it seems is talking about,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.900
you know, this humiliation for America

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.860
and that, you know, we haven't
been this humiliated since,

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.830
you know, Vietnam in Saigon.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.540
Do you, you know,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.480
is that in any way,
shape or form accurate?

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.440
I mean, do you feel humiliated

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.130
by the American militaries
leaving Afghanistan

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.690
or do you think that's a proper way

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.500
to be assessing what's going on right now?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.220
No, I think essentially
people are reacting

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.690
against what they assumed
was going to happen

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.410
which would be that the
Taliban would come in

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.460
and kill everybody

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:58.550
and that we'd have a horrible
black hawk down type disaster

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:01.840
as our guys try to get from
the embassy to the airport,

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.970
like some horrible
action movie or whatever.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.387
But they haven't done that.

00:03:05.387 --> 00:03:09.060
And the Taliban are,
they're obviously ruthless,

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.300
but oftentimes they
make rational decisions.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.133
You know what I mean?

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.150
Doesn't mean that their policy

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.060
is always just crazy.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.780
Essentially, they're not been modernized.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.613
You know what it is?

00:03:18.613 --> 00:03:20.980
I think people were thinking of

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.610
when ISIS took over Western Iraq

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.840
that it's gonna be like that.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.670
But the Taliban really aren't
Bin Laden-like lunatics

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.503
like that.

00:03:28.503 --> 00:03:32.110
They're very conservative
and extremely authoritarian

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:35.350
but they're not, you know,
revolutionaries really.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.320
Yeah and I guess they're
effectively they're state actors.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.540
I mean, you know exactly
who is in the Taliban now

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.460
and what the differences between

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.670
when it was actually running
Afghanistan before 9/11

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.470
or before the US invasion.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.580
But you know, they were government,

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.410
they're not a non-state actors.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.243
That's right.

00:03:56.243 --> 00:03:57.520
For many years they've called themselves

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.710
The Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.830
And they've acted as a shadow government

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.090
from the American side's point of view.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.010
But essentially as the
only real government

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.570
in much of the country for many years now.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.420
And even David Petraeus
at the height of the surge

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:15.000
or at the dawn of the surge
I guess, back 10 years ago,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.660
admitted that the Pashtun population,

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.670
especially in the south
and east of the country

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.550
and the predominantly Pashtun regions

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.810
that they vastly prefer

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:26.620
the Taliban system of
civil and criminal justice

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.970
to that imposed upon
them by the United States

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.390
and the new government
that we had set up there.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.630
And so.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.630
One of the arguments against Biden,

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.860
and I guess it's as much
against the, you know,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.670
the last 20 years of American
presence in Afghanistan

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:47.300
is that the way that the
withdrawal happened was,

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.810
you know, clearly we, you know,
there were a lot of people

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.670
who thought they were gonna get out.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.670
You know, there were,

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.830
one of the most disturbing
scenes I saw for, I guess,

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:57.930
was from over the weekend

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.960
were people were actually
hanging on to planes

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.020
as they were taking off.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:05.330
CNN was showing a guy who
apparently fell from a plane

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.480
that was a couple of
hundred feet up in the air.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.690
There is room to criticize the US

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.520
in the manner that it pulled out.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.353
Is there?

00:05:14.353 --> 00:05:16.720
Or where do you draw the
line on something like that?

